# 9. `toJson()`

Sometimes we need to send data **from Flutter to an API**.

Then we convert our Dart object into JSON.

Add:

```dart
Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {

  return {
    "id": id,
    "name": name,
    "email": email,
  };
}
```

Now:

```dart
final data = user.toJson();
```

Then:

```dart
final json = jsonEncode(data);
```

Flow:

```text
Flutter Object
      ↓
   toJson()
      ↓
    Map
      ↓
 jsonEncode()
      ↓
    JSON
      ↓
    API
```

---

# 10. Complete Model

```dart
class User {

  int id;
  String name;
  String email;

  User({
    required this.id,
    required this.name,
    required this.email,
  });

  factory User.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {

    return User(
      id: json["id"],
      name: json["name"],
      email: json["email"],
    );
  }

  Map<String, dynamic> toJson() {

    return {
      "id": id,
      "name": name,
      "email": email,
    };
  }
}
```

This is the basic pattern you should remember.

---

# 11. JSON Array

APIs often return multiple objects.

Example:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Rahul"
  },
  {
    "id": 2,
    "name": "Amit"
  },
  {
    "id": 3,
    "name": "Priya"
  }
]
```

After:

```dart
final data = jsonDecode(response.body);
```

`data` is a list.

Convert it into a list of `User` objects:

```dart
List<User> users = (data as List)
    .map((item) => User.fromJson(item))
    .toList();
```

Now:

```dart
users[0].name
users[1].name
users[2].name
```

---

# 12. JSON + ListView

This is a very common real-app flow:

```text
API
 ↓
JSON
 ↓
jsonDecode()
 ↓
List<User>
 ↓
ListView.builder()
 ↓
UI
```

Example:

```dart
ListView.builder(
  itemCount: users.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) {

    final user = users[index];

    return ListTile(
      title: Text(user.name),
      subtitle: Text(user.email),
    );
  },
)
```

This connects directly to the `ListView.builder` you already learned.

---

# 13. API + Model + FutureBuilder

For a real API:

```text
API
 ↓
http.get()
 ↓
response.body
 ↓
jsonDecode()
 ↓
User.fromJson()
 ↓
List<User>
 ↓
FutureBuilder
 ↓
ListView
```

This is one of the most important Flutter patterns for API-based apps.

